    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Description\n\nI have installed mini.icons (using vim.plug) and have require('mini.icons').setup() in my ~/.config/nvim/lua/init.lua (which is called from ~/.config/nvim/init.vim). I seem to have all the MiniIcons.* functions, but when I call them I get errors.\r\n\r\nI'm using mini.icons standalone, not the whole mini library.\r\n\r\nI have tried main and stable, same results with both.\r\n\r\nI am using urxvt as terminal. OS is Debian Testing.\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add `Plug 'echasnovski/mini.icons', { 'branch': 'stable' }` to ~/.config/nvim/init.vim\r\n2. Call :PlugInstall\r\n3. Add `require('mini.icons').setup()` to ~/.config/nvim/lua/init.vim\r\n4. Call :lua MiniIcons.list()\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA list of icons?\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua .../.local/share/nvim/plugged/mini.icons/lua/mini/icons.lua:496: attempt to concatenate local 'category' (a nil value)                                                                                     \r\nstack traceback:\r\n        .../.local/share/nvim/plugged/mini.icons/lua/mini/icons.lua:496: in function 'list'\r\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat am I doing wrong?\r\n\r\nHow can I verify if mini icons are working?",
