            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Judging by the error message, 'mini.icons' is set up and working. The issue is that [`MiniIcons.list()` takes a mandatory string `category` argument](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/7b4d5d48b6b5a75009d63f8f3e4ef4819b7e8139/doc/mini-icons.txt#L453). So you can verify with something like `:=MiniIcons.list('filetype')` (note using `:=` as it will print the output; just using `:lua MiniIcons.list('filetype')` will show nothing).",
